{#- Expects `interfaces`, `bgp` and `ospf` in scope.
    D: EOS routes nothing until `ip routing` is enabled globally (a `vrf instance` needs its own `ip routing vrf`, which
    arista_eos_vxlan.j2 renders). A device with no addressed interface, no BGP and no OSPF is a pure L2 switch and
    keeps routing off. -#}
{%- if interfaces | selectattr('ip_addresses') | list or bgp or ospf %}

! Enable IP routing
ip routing
{%- endif -%}
{#- U: IPv6 routing is a separate global switch on EOS (`ipv6 unicast-routing`); a VRF takes its own in
    arista_eos_vxlan.j2. Only a device with an IPv6 gateway SVI gets it. -#}
{%- if vlans | default([]) | selectattr('gateway_ipv6') | list %}

! Enable IPv6 routing
ipv6 unicast-routing
{%- endif -%}
